From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-geni: defer probe after transient GPI DMA failure

The S3706 touch controller is attached to the GENI I2C bus on
cc0000.geniqup / c80000.i2c.  On this board the GENI FIFO is disabled,
so the bus can only work through the shared GPI DMA controller.

During early boot the GPI controller can reject the first event-ring
allocation with a command-completion timeout.  dmaengine converts that
allocation failure into -ENODEV, and geni_i2c currently treats it as a
permanent probe failure.  The result is a boot with no touch input until
the next reboot:

  gpi c00000.dma-controller: cmd: EV ALLOCATE completion timeout:2
  gpi c00000.dma-controller: error alloc_ev_chan:-5
  geni_i2c c80000.i2c: error -ENODEV: Failed to get rx DMA ch

This is a probe-order/transient DMA resource failure, not a reason to
mark the I2C adapter permanently unusable.  When the device tree does
describe DMA channels, translate -ENODEV from dma_request_chan() into
-EPROBE_DEFER so the adapter is retried after the GPI controller has
finished initialising.  Devices without a DMA description keep the
existing hard failure behaviour.

Also release the transfer ring and reset the channel/GPII state when
gpi_ch_init() fails, otherwise each deferred probe leaks a coherent
transfer ring and leaves the GPII in a partially initialised state.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
@@ -1046,15 +1046,23 @@ static int setup_gpi_dma(struct geni_i2c_dev *gi2c)
 	geni_se_select_mode(&gi2c->se, GENI_GPI_DMA);
 	gi2c->tx_c = dma_request_chan(gi2c->se.dev, "tx");
 	if (IS_ERR(gi2c->tx_c)) {
-		ret = dev_err_probe(gi2c->se.dev, PTR_ERR(gi2c->tx_c),
-				    "Failed to get tx DMA ch\n");
+		ret = PTR_ERR(gi2c->tx_c);
+		if (ret == -ENODEV &&
+		    device_property_present(gi2c->se.dev, "dmas"))
+			ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		ret = dev_err_probe(gi2c->se.dev, ret,
+				    "Failed to get tx DMA ch\n");
 		goto err_tx;
 	}
 
 	gi2c->rx_c = dma_request_chan(gi2c->se.dev, "rx");
 	if (IS_ERR(gi2c->rx_c)) {
-		ret = dev_err_probe(gi2c->se.dev, PTR_ERR(gi2c->rx_c),
-				    "Failed to get rx DMA ch\n");
+		ret = PTR_ERR(gi2c->rx_c);
+		if (ret == -ENODEV &&
+		    device_property_present(gi2c->se.dev, "dmas"))
+			ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		ret = dev_err_probe(gi2c->se.dev, ret,
+				    "Failed to get rx DMA ch\n");
 		goto err_rx;
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
@@ -2065,7 +2065,15 @@ static int gpi_alloc_chan_resources(struct dma_chan *chan)
 		goto xfer_alloc_err;
 
 	ret = gpi_ch_init(gchan);
+	if (ret) {
+		gpi_free_ring(&gchan->ch_ring, gpii);
+		write_lock_irq(&gpii->pm_lock);
+		gchan->pm_state = DISABLE_STATE;
+		if (gpii->pm_state == PREPARE_HARDWARE)
+			gpii->pm_state = DISABLE_STATE;
+		write_unlock_irq(&gpii->pm_lock);
+	}
 
 	mutex_unlock(&gpii->ctrl_lock);
 
 	return ret;
